  "notes": "{弾|ひ}く is used for playing stringed and keyboard instruments where keys or strings are pressed/plucked.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{弾|ひ}く\n\nAPPLIES TO:\n- ⟦ピアノ→ピアノ：01376_piano⟧: piano\n- ⟦ギター→ギター：04461_gitaa⟧: guitar\n- ⟦バイオリン→バイオリン：00009_baiorin⟧: violin\n- ⟦{三味線|しゃみせん}→三味線：04464_shamisen⟧: shamisen\n\nINSTRUMENT VERB DISTINCTIONS:\n- {弾|ひ}く: stringed/keyboard (piano, guitar)\n- ⟦{吹|ふ}く→吹く：02445_fuku⟧: wind instruments (flute, trumpet)\n- ⟦{叩|たた}く→叩く：02072_tataku⟧/⟦{打|う}つ→打つ：01221_utsu⟧: percussion (drums)\n- ⟦{演奏|えんそう}する→演奏する：20349_ensousuru⟧: to perform (any instrument, formal)\n\nUSAGE:\nDo not confuse with other verbs read as ひく:\n- ⟦{引|ひ}く→引く：01978_hiku⟧: to pull\n- ⟦{惹|ひ}く→惹く：27838_hiku⟧: to attract",
